    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d857">

                <pb facs="0793" n="781" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg781"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R.–Subs/6: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Messersmith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-17T12:00:00-04:00">June 17,
                            1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 12:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>65. Department’s circular June 13, 8 p.m. Secretary of State said that he would
                    add to Cuba’s neutrality legislation a provision excluding belligerent
                    submarines from Cuban ports and territorial waters similar to that contained in
                    the proclamation of the President of the United States of November 4, 1939.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Messersmith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
